---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site
  title="Privacy & licenses"
  description="Website privacy, external services and AirHound component licenses."
>
  <header class="page-header wrap">
    <h1>Privacy & licenses.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The project website is a static guide. It does not receive your wireless
      observations.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="wrap content prose">
    <h2>Website privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This site includes no application analytics, advertising trackers, account
      system or capture-upload endpoint. Documentation search runs against a
      local static index. Fonts are served with the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your browser still requests website files from the hosting provider. The
      production provider and its request-log policy must be documented before
      launch. Following a GitHub link takes you to GitHub, whose own privacy
      policy applies. Download assets are hosted on GitHub Releases.
    </p>
    <p>
      Examples use synthetic or sanitized information. Please keep identifying
      observations out of public issue reports and screenshots.
    </p>
    <p>
      Self-hosted typefaces: <a href="/licenses/manrope.txt">Manrope license</a>{" "}
      and <a href="/licenses/newsreader.txt">Newsreader license</a> (SIL Open
      Font License).
    </p>
    <h2 id="licenses">Different components, explicit licenses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/dougborg/AirHound/blob/main/LICENSE">
          AirHound project: MIT
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/dougborg/AirHound/tree/main/drivers/mt7610u">
          Independent MT7610U receiver: GPL-2.0-only, with component notices and
          corresponding source
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/dougborg/AirHound/blob/main/scripts/sniffle-source.py">
          Sniffle source helper: GPL-3.0-only
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/dougborg/AirHound/tree/main/website">
          Website source and third-party dependency notices
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      External radio firmware and upstream Sniffle tools are installed
      separately. A signature’s inclusion does not settle every upstream data
      provenance question; consult its review metadata.
    </p>
  </div>
</Site>
